The optional `rustleaks-connections-v1` rules adapt the five first-party
Kingfisher definitions at commit
`01e7b817376fbf2272be8f162bd32309bf97ee1f`.

Copyright 2025-2026 MongoDB, Inc.
https://www.mongodb.com

Source repository: https://github.com/mongodb/kingfisher

These rule assets retain the Apache License, Version 2.0; its exact text is
included in the adjacent `LICENSE.kingfisher`. Rustleaks changes identifiers,
descriptions, regex notation and ASCII scope, maps all source substring
exclusions to secret stopwords, and unrolls the bounded JDBC option repetition.
Original patterns, transformations and source hashes are recorded in the
adjacent `rustleaks-connections-v1.provenance.json`. This pack includes no
Kingfisher scanner implementation. The separately attributed URI rule above
is derived from Betterleaks; its provenance records the reviewed Kingfisher
overlay and its inapplicability to database schemes.

The optional `rustleaks-providers-v1` pack also adapts four finite Veles
(OSV-SCALIBR) token expressions from commit
`e8621f1fff93beb5b70e5d6ba5fdc3e9854ec845`:
https://github.com/google/osv-scalibr

Copyright 2026 Google LLC
Copyright 2025 Google LLC (additional xAI source header)

These expressions retain the Apache License, Version 2.0, whose exact source
text is included in the adjacent `LICENSE.veles`. The pinned archive records
no upstream NOTICE. Rustleaks changes identifiers and descriptions, wraps the
complete token in capture 1, and uses its existing source and finding policy.
No network validators or scanner implementation are included. The adjacent
`rustleaks-providers-v1.provenance.json` records individual source paths,
pattern lines, hashes, finite lengths and the xAI source-selection decision.
